    "notes": "PMTiles identifies the historic wings, concourse roof and west rail yard. The mapped hall axis sets the heading. Nine entrance probes, four public hall probes and sixteen rail lanes clear the authored geometry. The historic wings, main hall, west shed and centerlines use PMTiles plan geometry. Window, truss, roof and architectural sections are reconstructed from the photos. Terrain supplies approach elevations. The interior concourse and rail bed heights are reconstructed from standard terrain samples and visible station connections. The model represents the public ground-level concourses and western train hall. Underground tracks, shops, interiors beyond the public hall and moving trains are outside its scope."
